<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hosea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hosea was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> prophet in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a> in the 8th century BCE, during its last decades before the Assyrian conquest. The biblical Book of Hosea uses his marriage to an unfaithful wife as an image of Israel's unfaithfulness to its God, condemning the worship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baal">Baal</a> and alliances with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. It is the first of the twelve Minor Prophets.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hosea.jpg" alt="Hosea" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Tissot · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hosea_by_James_Tissot_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…population of the Kingdom of Israel, the &quot;Ten Lost Tribes&quot; of biblical tradition, profoundly marked the history of Israel and Judah; the Assyrian crisis is reflected in the prophetic books of Isaiah, <b>Hosea</b> and Micah, and in the biblical account of Sennacherib's siege of Jerusalem in 701 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>In the prosperous eighth century wealth gathered in the hands of the court and great landowners, and the prophets Amos and <b>Hosea</b> denounced the luxury of Samaria, the oppression of the poor and the worship of other gods.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in the United Kingdom of Israel. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safed">Safed</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=32.97,35.5&amp;year=-735" aria-label="Safed on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5459 966 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Hosea"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5909 1236h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5909 1236h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=32.97,35.5&amp;year=-735">What was here in 735 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="enc-words" id="in-their-words"><h2 class="enc-section-title">In their words</h2><blockquote class="enc-q"><p>&#8220;For they have sown the wind, and they shall reap the whirlwind…&#8221;</p><footer>Hosea 8:7 &#183; King James Version, 1611 &#183; <a href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Bible_(King_James)/Hosea" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a></footer></blockquote><blockquote class="enc-q"><p>&#8220;For I desired mercy, and not sacrifice; and the knowledge of God more than burnt offerings.&#8221;</p><footer>Hosea 6:6 &#183; King James Version, 1611 &#183; the prophet speaking in the name of God &#183; <a href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Bible_(King_James)/Hosea" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a></footer></blockquote><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/encyclopedia/quotations">Quotations from 535 people &rarr;</a></p></section>
